  "body": "**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\nNot so much a problem as an improvement for Meshtastic to be better at doing CAD:\nIn two cases we need the receiver re-armed *without* dropping a packet already on the air: \n1) CAD with a GOTO_RX exit mode — the chip auto-enters RX to catch the packet CAD just detected;\n2) re-arming the DIO interrupt after `RX_DONE` in continuous RX while a second packet is still arriving.\n\nEvery route back into RX goes through `startReceive()` → `stageMode(RX)`, which `standby()`s (SX126x/LR11x0) or clears IRQ + re-issues `setRx` (LR2021). All of these abort the in-flight reception, so LBT can't hand a detected packet to the normal RX path.\n\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\nAdd `PhysicalLayer::resumeReceive(startRx=false, irqFlags, irqMask)` basically remapping the RX IRQ and optionally re-issue `setRx`, with no preceding `standby()` for SX126x, LR11x0, LR2021 (CAD-exit-mode radios).\n\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\nYou could make the supporting functions public rather than private, or we could run in godmode.\n\n**Additional context**\nI have a drafted branch ready to go at https://github.com/NomDeTom/RadioLib/tree/rxResume, and a rather more verbose PR in with meshtastic so you can see the proposed implementation at work: https://github.com/meshtastic/firmware/pull/11137\n\nFinal disclosure: I leant heavily on Claude Code for this, but I believe the code matches the rest of the codebase and I've reviewed it as best I can.\n",
